  "description": "issue #782 (the self-heal path): a turtle command issued AFTER a callee's `tell` applies to the newly addressed turtle. `go` runs `tell :b`, then the caller's `forward 40` moves :b — one `move`/`draw-segment` pair carrying `turtle_id: 2`, the acting turtle's identity (`spec/turtles-and-sprites.md:46,113`) — and `who`/`ycor` then agree on :b at y 40. This is the path that made the defect intermittent and position-dependent: the next turtle command re-derived the stale per-`Environment` cache from the shared pointer and hid the divergence, so the wrong answer was only observable in the window between the call returning and the next turtle command. Pinning the healed state here means a regression cannot be masked by simply running one more command.",
